{:answer/id #uuid "6b256a66-dffd-5744-a8cd-388957d080dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515769} {:answer/id #uuid "6c073a98-13c7-5c27-9d53-fc967682b24f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515770} {:answer/id #uuid "cb639f57-2b8d-5292-89c5-d5105f866b73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515789} {:answer/id #uuid "cf745f86-8585-5069-a02e-7ae9b862f9d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515790} {:answer/id #uuid "d6931356-36dc-52f2-a09f-5e9d078eed60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6931356-36dc-52f2-a09f-5e9d078eed60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515794} :answer-field/id #uuid "13afb8d0-e29c-5e03-8275-97617083d5a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515741}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "90ae461d-564d-5a00-970d-e4fcb1014552" :question/problem "If $tan⁡x=-8,$ then $\\frac{1}{8}tan⁡(-x-7\\pi )+3=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/df/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x-7\\pi ) & =tan⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x) & =-tan⁡x \\\\  & =-(-8) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8}tan⁡(-x-7\\pi )+3 & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 8+3 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{8}+3 \\\\  & =1+3 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515793 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e858aee-aaf3-5d29-b8bd-ade58fa7d13f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{59}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515739} {:answer/id #uuid "3906c88a-6cae-5eae-a3e4-0a590c5f854a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515749} {:answer/id #uuid "42e6e239-6429-513a-845b-06a06182439d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515756} {:answer/id #uuid "8fa7169a-7e10-59d1-b9c9-bb98ee7d9981" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515777} {:answer/id #uuid "b653017b-5c45-5ebc-ab75-53d6c1b84da6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42e6e239-6429-513a-845b-06a06182439d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515756} :answer-field/id #uuid "65b32ad3-3562-5293-912b-f6dcacf94d48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515765}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d4e8bdc3-e66f-5636-b57f-ea5c00423763" :question/problem "If $tan⁡x=-7,$ then $\\frac{7}{8}tan⁡(-x+\\pi )+\\frac{3}{8}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/df/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x+\\pi ) & =tan⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x) & =-tan⁡x \\\\  & =-(-7) \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{8}tan⁡(-x+\\pi )+\\frac{3}{8} & =\\frac{7}{8}\\cdot 7+\\frac{3}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{49}{8}+\\frac{3}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{52}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515803 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bbbdfef-ff18-5840-a720-bf3a6e3607ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4} + 6π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515752} {:answer/id #uuid "543421b3-6f98-5b39-8bf2-a75be506ac0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515761} {:answer/id #uuid "a1c4bac2-ad78-587b-af3a-667ee44fb5ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515783} {:answer/id #uuid "d814092d-bfbb-5323-a7b1-522b7df39eff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515796} {:answer/id #uuid "deab0bda-34c3-53e6-babc-d4b07ef2a1d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4} + 6π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515798}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1c4bac2-ad78-587b-af3a-667ee44fb5ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515783} :answer-field/id #uuid "f15360d1-03e2-5d57-9abe-a5cfabf7bc07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515804}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f09b88d6-2fb6-5a40-9a66-3a39d967393d" :question/problem "If $\\tan x = \\frac{7}{4}$, then $\\tan (-x + 6π) =$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/df/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x+6\\pi ) & =tan⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x) & =-tan⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\tan (-x + 6π)=-\\frac{7}{4}.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Oddness Property of the Tangent Function"}]}
